course: dictionary
lesson: 3051
title: Which way is eastward?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Eastward is a direction word. It tells you that something moves or faces towards the east. «The ship sailed eastward» means the ship went towards the east.
explain: Eastward can also describe a thing, like a road. «The eastward road» is a road that goes towards the east. Look at the ending: -ward means "in the direction of", as in homeward or upward.
explain: On a normal map, north is at the top and east is on the right. So moving eastward means moving to the right. The sun seems to rise in the east because the Earth spins eastward.
explain: Time can go eastward too. «Crossing the International Date Line westwards you jump forward one calendar day, and crossing it eastwards you go back one day.» Going eastward across that line takes you back a day.
fact: Eastward means towards the east.
fact: Eastward can be an adverb, telling you where something goes, or an adjective, describing a road or a direction.
fact: Eastwards means the same as eastward when it is used as an adverb.
fact: On a normal map, moving eastward means moving to the right.
fact: The Earth spins eastward, which is why the sun seems to rise in the east.
exercise: «The ship sailed eastward across the calm sea.» What does eastward mean here? | *Towards the east | Towards the north | Very slowly | Under the water
exercise: In «the eastward road», eastward describes the road. What kind of word is it? | *An adjective, because it describes the road | A verb | A question word
exercise: On a normal map, which way is eastward? | Up the page | Down the page | To the left | *To the right
test: Which phrase means moving to the right on a normal map? | Move southward | *Move eastward | Move upward | Stand still
test: The sun seems to rise in the east because the Earth spins which way? | *Eastward | Backward | Upward | Westward
exam: «Crossing the International Date Line eastwards» takes you across a line on the map. What happens to the day when you cross it eastwards? | The day lasts a whole week | You jump forward one day | The day stays the same | *You go back one day
